    left, all, ...), or ends in -ly / -ed: strongest;
  - another standalone word: medium; a prefix such as non-, anti-, pre-, co-, re-: weaker;
  - a bare number ("3-"): weak to medium;
  - a fragment of a word split by a hyphen (line-break style "em-ployees"): weak;
  - a LaTeX "$" before the hyphen: very strong.
A hyphen with a space before it (" - ") does not fire. A run of middle dots "····" gives a
large negative value, as seen in one degenerate training row.
Bare hyphen tokens ("-") fire more than hyphen-plus-word tokens ("-year").
